{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix pushed for review: Gerrit change 2558 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2558 (commit 437d8790c632, branch reb-febd-uv-pin, 5 files +235/-4).\n\n## The diagnosis was reproduced locally, not merely inferred\n\nBuilding `Dockerfile.opcert` with `:latest` and `--no-cache` reproduced the production failure verbatim: `error: Required uv version ==0.12.7 does not match the running version 0.12.9`, exit code 2. After the fix the same build exits 0, resolves `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.12.7@sha256:95f2aa1f...`, completes `uv sync --locked`, and `docker run --entrypoint uv` reports `uv 0.12.7 (aarch64-unknown-linux-musl)`. Only opcert was built (smallest); mcp and reviewbot carry the identical COPY line and the identical fix.\n\n## AC3 gate written FIRST and seen RED\n\n    FAILED test_real_repository_dockerfiles_do_not_float_the_uv_tag\n      AssertionError: floating :latest toolchain tags: [\n        'infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:90',\n        'infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert:37',\n        'infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:112']\n    FAILED test_real_repository_dockerfiles_match_the_pyproject_pin\n    FAILED test_dockerfile_floating_uv_tag_is_rejected\n    FAILED test_dockerfile_uv_tag_skewed_from_pyproject_is_rejected\n    FAILED test_dockerfile_untagged_uv_reference_is_rejected\n    FAILED test_dockerfile_floating_base_image_is_rejected\n    6 failed, 20 passed\n\nAll three offenders flagged, and the four fixture tests confirm the gate previously had NO Dockerfile coverage at all.\n\n## AC2 — no new mechanism was added\n\n`scripts/check_uv_pin.py` already existed, already parses `[tool.uv] required-version` from pyproject.toml, exists for exactly this defect class on the CI side, and is already wired into `make lint`. It was EXTENDED rather than duplicated. It now fails on a uv tag differing from required-version (naming both versions), on any floating `:latest`, and on an omitted tag (an omitted tag IS `:latest`), while allowing named build stages, stage indices, and `@sha256:` digest pins. `make lint`'s mechanism-delta ratchet confirms new=0.\n\nRejected alternatives, recorded so this is not relitigated:\n- **ARG UV_VERSION from compose** — the compose build blocks have no `args:` today, so it needs new plumbing AND autodeploy.sh must preserve it; worse, a plain `docker build -f Dockerfile.mcp .` falls back to the ARG default, so the literal still lives in each Dockerfile plus a second copy in compose. Strictly more places to drift.\n- **A new .github/uv-version.txt** (mirroring module-size-limit.txt) — pyproject's required-version is ALREADY the single source; uv reads it directly and it is what actually fails the build. A second file makes two sources of truth needing their own equality gate — the same problem one level up. The module-size-limit.txt precedent applies where no canonical declaration exists; here one does.\n- **Bumping required-version to 0.12.9** — rejected per AC; it fixes nothing, because the images would still float and break at the next upstream release.\n\n## Blast radius — full sweep\n\nFixed: the three uv lines. Already clean: every other image reference — python:3.12-slim (x3), gerritcodereview/gerrit:3.14.1, and tests/external/live_jira_dc/Dockerfile (digest-pinned).\n\nCorrectly NOT flagged: `:latest` in autodeploy.sh and the runbooks refers to LOCAL image tags (compose-review-bot:latest, $MCP_IMAGE:latest) used for the :prev/:latest rollback dance. Locally produced, cannot float; a `_is_registry_reference` split keeps them out.\n\nONE ITEM LEFT DELIBERATELY OUT OF SCOPE, needing a decision: `docker-compose.langfuse.yml:113` runs `image: docker.io/minio/minio:latest`. Same defect class, but it is a compose `image:` key rather than a Dockerfile, so AC3 as written does not cover it, and choosing a MinIO version could not be validated here. Lower blast radius (dev/observability stack, no build gate depends on it). Widening the gate to compose `image:` keys is a small follow-up if wanted.\n\n## Verification\n\ntest_uv_pin_guard.py 26 passed; `-k \"docker or uv or pin or image\"` 601 passed / 6 skipped; MCP + opcert infra suites 76 passed; make lint exit 0; make typecheck Success across 744 files; verify-commit-ticket OK.\n\n## Recovery note\n\nLanding this does not by itself clear the 502. It restores the ability to BUILD; the MCP container is separately dead (OOM, bug 9ea3), so the endpoint recovers only once autodeploy completes a successful rebuild and cutover. AC4 (deployed-sha advancing to current origin/main) is the confirmation to watch."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788412833220817001,"uuid":"23f11e56-0615-4d98-95b2-e01f16e5e6e5"}